================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

Reverie redistributes the pinned native sources used by its optional backends
inside their Cargo packages:

  * `reverie-dbt/vendor/dynamorio`
  * `experimental/reverie-sabre/vendor/{sabre,libelf}`
  * `reverie-e9patch/vendor/e9patch`

The `third-party/` git submodules remain developer reference checkouts, but the
Cargo builds do not read them. The complete license texts named below are part
of the corresponding vendored source trees and therefore part of each source
package.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DynamoRIO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:  https://github.com/DynamoRIO/dynamorio
Fork:      https://github.com/rrnewton/dynamorio
Pinned commit: 929840ad9190e5086775e8debc0f0b79b4208d59
Packaged path: `reverie-dbt/vendor/dynamorio`
License:   BSD-3-Clause (primary), with the additional component licenses below.
           Full text: `reverie-dbt/vendor/dynamorio/License.txt`.

  Copyright (c) 2010-2024 Google, Inc.   All rights reserved.
  Copyright (c) 2000-2009 VMware, Inc.   All rights reserved.

DynamoRIO's License.txt calls out non-BSD-3 portions. The curated build uses
`BUILD_CLIENTS=OFF`, `BUILD_EXT=ON`, and `BUILD_TOOLS=ON`, and retains only
drcontainers, drmgr, drreg, drwrap, and drx. Of those packaged extensions,
drwrap is LGPL-2.1-only; its complete text is also at
`reverie-dbt/vendor/dynamorio/ext/drwrap/license.txt`.

The curated tree does not contain drsyms, drsyscall, drutil, elfutils, libipt,
or zlib sources.

The curated tree also omits upstream's documentation and Windows-resource
images (`api/docs/genimages/*.png`, `api/docs/images/*`, `tools/DRinstall/res/*`,
`tools/DRstats/res/*`). They are documentation assets that no build step reads,
and this repository does not carry binary files. Their removal changes no
licensing: they are covered by the same DynamoRIO BSD-3-Clause grant above,
whose complete text remains packaged.

The packaged tree also contains:

  * third_party/valgrind headers
    (valgrind.h, memcheck.h) ............. BSD-4-Clause
                                           Copyright (C) 2000-2013 Julian Seward.
    The full BSD-4-Clause notice is embedded at the top of each header under
    `reverie-dbt/vendor/dynamorio/third_party/valgrind/`.

