e9patch
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:  https://github.com/GJDuck/e9patch
Pinned commit: 6c2c03c1da74b14daf1788a9f8dccfa354ce04a6 (v1.0.1)
Packaged path: `reverie-e9patch/vendor/e9patch`
License:   GPL-3.0-only (primary; complete text in `LICENSE`), with the bundled
           libdw subset used under LGPL-3.0-or-later (complete text in
           `contrib/libdw/COPYING-LGPLV3`) and Zydis under MIT (complete text in
           `contrib/zydis/LICENSE`).

The curated tree omits upstream's `.github/e9patch.png` project logo, because
this repository does not carry binary files.

e9tool only decodes and formats instructions, so the packaged Zydis is built
with upstream's `ZYDIS_DISABLE_ENCODER` switch and the encoder sources are not
redistributed: `contrib/zydis/src/Encoder.c`, `src/EncoderData.c`,
`include/Zydis/Encoder.h`, `include/Zydis/Internal/EncoderData.h`, and the
generated `src/Generated/EncoderTables.inc` (2.6 MB). None of them was ever in
the `contrib/zydis` object list. The Zydis MIT text stays packaged in full and
covers the retained decoder, formatter, and generated decoder tables.
